@model EmploymentStatus

@*
    One employment status, named in the reader's language.

    A partial rather than @T[status.ToString()] at each of the four places that shows one. That form
    compiles and renders the enum member — "OnLeave" — and is invisible to
    LocalisationResourceTests, which looks for string literals: every status would have no resource
    entry, no translation, and nothing to report it. It came in with session A2 and is the same
    defect as the lifecycle labels, found the same way.

    The switch is exhaustive over the enum with no default, so adding a status is a compiler error
    here rather than an English word on an Arabic screen.
*@

<span class="badge bg-secondary employee-status">@(Model switch
{
    EmploymentStatus.Prospective => T["Prospective"],
    EmploymentStatus.Active => T["Active"],
    EmploymentStatus.OnLeave => T["On leave"],
    EmploymentStatus.Suspended => T["Suspended"],
    EmploymentStatus.Exited => T["Exited"],
    _ => T["Unknown"],
})</span>
